<figure class="gridding-diagram" aria-labelledby="gridding-diagram-title">
  <figcaption id="gridding-diagram-title">
    Physical grid cells and local Bernstein coefficient labels
  </figcaption>

  <section class="diagram-panel">
    <h3>One parameter: two cells, degree 2</h3>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 210" role="img" aria-label="A one-dimensional grid has nodes rho zero, rho one, rho two and two physical cells. Each degree-two cell stores three local Bernstein coefficients.">
      <text x="380" y="23" text-anchor="middle" class="caption">grid nodes partition the physical parameter interval</text>
      <line x1="92" y1="80" x2="668" y2="80" class="axis" />
      <rect x="92" y="56" width="288" height="48" class="cell selected" />
      <rect x="380" y="56" width="288" height="48" class="cell" />
      <g class="node">
        <circle cx="92" cy="80" r="7" />
        <circle cx="380" cy="80" r="7" />
        <circle cx="668" cy="80" r="7" />
      </g>
      <g class="math-label">
        <text x="92" y="129" text-anchor="middle">ρ₀</text>
        <text x="380" y="129" text-anchor="middle">ρ₁</text>
        <text x="668" y="129" text-anchor="middle">ρ₂</text>
      </g>
      <text x="236" y="92" text-anchor="middle" class="cell-label">physical cell 1</text>
      <text x="524" y="92" text-anchor="middle" class="cell-label">physical cell 2</text>
      <path d="M236 108 V141" class="guide" />
      <path d="M524 108 V141" class="guide" />
      <g class="coefficient-row">
        <rect x="138" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <rect x="204" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <rect x="270" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <text x="170" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽¹⁾[0]</text>
        <text x="236" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽¹⁾[1]</text>
        <text x="302" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽¹⁾[2]</text>
        <rect x="426" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <rect x="492" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <rect x="558" y="149" width="64" height="35" rx="5" />
        <text x="458" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽²⁾[0]</text>
        <text x="524" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽²⁾[1]</text>
        <text x="590" y="172" text-anchor="middle">C⁽²⁾[2]</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <p>
      Three grid nodes create <strong>two physical cells</strong>. Degree 2
      gives <strong>three local Bernstein labels</strong> per cell; it does
      not add grid nodes. A global coefficient grid shares the boundary
      handle, so <code>C^(1)[2] = C^(2)[0]</code> at the interface.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="diagram-panel">
    <h3>Two parameters: unequal node counts, degree 1</h3>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 320" role="img" aria-label="A two-dimensional four by three node grid creates six physical rectangular cells. The highlighted cell contains four degree-one tensor Bernstein coefficient labels.">
      <text x="250" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="caption">physical tensor grid</text>
      <g class="grid2d">
        <rect x="82" y="55" width="336" height="204" class="cell" />
        <line x1="194" y1="55" x2="194" y2="259" />
        <line x1="306" y1="55" x2="306" y2="259" />
        <line x1="82" y1="157" x2="418" y2="157" />
        <rect x="194" y="157" width="112" height="102" class="selected" />
      </g>
      <g class="math-label">
        <text x="82" y="282" text-anchor="middle">ρ₁,₀</text>
        <text x="194" y="282" text-anchor="middle">ρ₁,₁</text>
        <text x="306" y="282" text-anchor="middle">ρ₁,₂</text>
        <text x="418" y="282" text-anchor="middle">ρ₁,₃</text>
        <text x="63" y="60" text-anchor="end">ρ₂,₂</text>
        <text x="63" y="162" text-anchor="end">ρ₂,₁</text>
        <text x="63" y="264" text-anchor="end">ρ₂,₀</text>
      </g>
      <text x="250" y="214" text-anchor="middle" class="cell-label">cell c = [2, 1]</text>
      <path d="M322 208 H454" class="guide" />
      <text x="578" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="caption">one selected cell: local labels</text>
      <g class="local-cell">
        <rect x="500" y="55" width="156" height="156" />
        <line x1="578" y1="55" x2="578" y2="211" />
        <line x1="500" y1="133" x2="656" y2="133" />
        <text x="539" y="98" text-anchor="middle">[0, 1]</text>
        <text x="617" y="98" text-anchor="middle">[1, 1]</text>
        <text x="539" y="176" text-anchor="middle">[0, 0]</text>
        <text x="617" y="176" text-anchor="middle">[1, 0]</text>
      </g>
      <text x="578" y="242" text-anchor="middle" class="caption">(Degree + 1)² = 4 coefficients</text>
    </svg>
    <p>
      A 4-by-3 node grid makes 3-by-2 physical cells, showing that axis node
      counts need not match. Degree 1 is applied in
      <em>each</em> parameter direction, so a selected cell stores the four
      tensor labels <code>[0 0]</code>, <code>[0 1]</code>,
      <code>[1 0]</code>, and <code>[1 1]</code> in package order.
    </p>
  </section>
</figure>

